Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Undetermined", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"0556612f-982e-4e7c-b41b-7cde16fd3edf"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Undetermined"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/Undetermined", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "258b989b-92ce-49ba-8e35-e151ae7b4e88"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is the value of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["graph", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["obj", "TI"], ",", " ", "\"\<Faithful\>\""}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e96244a-d017-4b4b-a30c-a3e5ca684c38"],
 " on a head whose graph is faithful \[LongDash] its chains are exactly its \
intended members \[LongDash] only under a hypothesis this paclet does not \
certify.",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"9b835f8f-7da8-4dbe-b55d-ba3f3ef861b7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every Euclidean head has a graph, and \"Faithful\" states whether every \
chain of that graph is genuinely a member of the head and every member a \
chain of it. For a segment, a ray or a line this is a proved theorem and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Faithful\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e2571d47-18cb-4f05-af72-df7c2fa9a850"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "270ea1b0-b46b-4196-9823-d531872b0fad"],
 ". For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraCircle"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraCircle", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "fdc6670d-9e2b-45d6-97a8-e6421ec08af4"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraArc"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraArc", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "457d1da6-6799-42a7-8230-0cc4190db45c"],
 " the analogous statement needs a geometric hypothesis on the substrate \
\[LongDash] for the circle the winding functional (W) and the one-run \
hypothesis (T), for the arc (W) together with ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 " lying on a common circle \[LongDash] that no computation here checks, so \
the honest answer is neither ",
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cd37ff39-5768-4899-ac71-f676fa8fe9fc"],
 " nor ",
 Cell[BoxData["False"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "92648be3-3b43-44b0-b5ea-13c4fff8823f"],
 " but ",
 Cell[BoxData["Undetermined"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01d411f9-b3bb-4a8f-8d08-f0a497716cee"],
 ": the question is open on this call, not answered no."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ecf33c3d-877d-4834-b417-7bbc21393212"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["Undetermined"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6c9906f9-bf0c-40ff-97e6-77bba2e87b9f"],
 " carries no further structure; it is a plain symbol, not a function."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4cca23cf-f9f7-4a80-8e54-964499ed6690"]
}, Open  ]],

